.TH NVFLUX 1 2026-10-23 "nvflux 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nvflux \- lock NVIDIA GPU memory and graphics clocks, safely
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nvflux
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The NVIDIA driver keeps raising and lowering the GPU clocks.
Each change of the memory clock can cause HDMI/DisplayPort audio crackle,
screen flicker or a short stutter; a graphics clock that ramps up slowly makes
the desktop lag; a clock that boosts higher than needed makes noise and heat.
.B nvflux
holds the clocks where they need to be.
.PP
It only uses NVIDIA's own clock-lock functions and only clock values the
driver reports as supported.
The driver's power limit and thermal protection stay in force.
It never overclocks, changes voltages, power limits or fans.
.PP
The chosen mode is saved and applied again at boot and after sleep.
Before the system sleeps, the locks are released, so the GPU goes through
sleep in the driver's default state.
.SH MODES
.TP
.B balanced
Holds memory at the lowest clock that doesn't limit the graphics clock, and
keeps the graphics clock above 45% of its maximum.
Fixes audio crackle, flicker and desktop lag.
The usual choice.
.TP
.B powersave
Holds memory like
.BR balanced ,
and caps the graphics clock at the card's base clock.
Cooler, quieter, less power.
.TP
.B max
Holds memory at its highest clock; graphics boosts freely.
For games and compute.
Uses more power when idle.
.TP
.B off
The driver controls the clocks again.
.PP
GPUs that can't lock their memory clock (before RTX 30) get the graphics part
of each mode.
GPUs before GTX 16/RTX 20 can't lock clocks at all.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B status
Mode, current clocks, what nvflux locks them at, power and temperature.
The default command.
.TP
.B info
The clocks each GPU supports, and what each mode would set.
.TP
.B doctor
Checks the driver, permissions, hooks and the applied mode.
Prints one line per check (ok, warn or FAIL) with the fix.
.TP
.B reload
Applies the saved mode again.
Run by the boot and sleep hooks.
.TP
.BI "lock memory " MHz
Holds the memory clock at the supported clock nearest to
.IR MHz .
.TP
.BI "lock graphics " MHz | min - max
Holds the graphics clock at one clock or within a range.
.IP
Values snap to the nearest supported clock.
A memory clock that limits the graphics clock, or a graphics cap below 45% of
the maximum, needs
.BR \-\-force .
Locks are saved like a mode.
.TP
.BR help ", " version
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-temporary
Applies a mode or lock without saving it.
The saved mode comes back at the next reboot, sleep or
.BR reload .
.TP
.BI \-\-gpu " N"
Only GPU
.I N
(numbered as in
.BR status ).
Saved by the GPU's UUID.
.TP
.B \-\-force
With
.BR lock :
allow a lock that slows the GPU down.
.TP
.B \-\-json
With
.B status
and
.BR info :
machine-readable output.
Fields are only ever added, never renamed or removed.
.SH PERMISSIONS
nvflux is installed setuid root, mode 4750, group
.BR nvflux .
Members of the group can change clocks without sudo; others use
.BR sudo .
Commands that only read give root up before doing anything.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/nvflux
The program.
.TP
.I /var/lib/nvflux/state
The saved mode.
.TP
.I /var/lib/nvflux/installed
What the installer installed; used by
.B doctor
and
.BR uninstall.sh .
.TP
.I /run/nvflux/current
A
.B \-\-temporary
mode; cleared at boot.
.SH KERNEL COMMAND LINE
.TP
.B nvflux=off
.B reload
does nothing.
Use it to boot without nvflux's locks.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
Failed, or a value was refused.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error.
.TP
.B 3
No permission.
.TP
.B 4
Not supported by this GPU or driver.
.TP
.B 5
Applied to some GPUs, not all.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
nvflux balanced
nvflux max \-\-temporary
nvflux lock memory 5001
nvflux lock graphics 900\-1800
nvflux status \-\-json
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR nvidia\-smi (1)
